cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "eljazari.ai: a multi-agent system for drone design, code generation and simulated flight test"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata. The bundled AircraftVerse design data is a separate work under CC-BY-4.0 and must be cited independently — see references below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ezzaldin
    family-names: Hamed
    alias: ezzhamed
repository-code: "https://github.com/ezzhamed/eljazari.ai"
abstract: >-
  eljazari.ai turns a natural-language request for a multirotor and its mission,
  in English or Arabic, into a design and bill of materials from a component
  catalogue, a flight model of that aircraft estimated from manufacturer motor
  tests, PX4/MAVSDK mission code checked by a safety layer and approved by a
  person, and a PX4 SITL + Gazebo flight that a deterministic gate accepts only
  if it flew the approved mission. LLM agents coordinated by a LangGraph
  orchestrator write the design and the code. Results are software-in-the-loop
  simulation only, not calibration, hardware testing or airworthiness.
keywords:
  - multi-agent-systems
  - large-language-models
  - langgraph
  - uav
  - drone-design
  - px4
  - gazebo
  - mavsdk
  - software-in-the-loop
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - ai-safety
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0-alpha.1
